### Platform access API manual requests
# Start the API with ConnectionStrings:PlatformDatabase (or PLATFORM_DB_CONNECTION), configure the
# Authentication:Issuer, Audience, and a 32-byte-or-longer SigningKey, and apply the EF migrations first.
# Use the seeded product IDs below. Catalog administration still requires a PlatformAdmin JWT.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@adminToken = replace-with-platform-admin-jwt
@ownerToken = replace-with-tenant-owner-jwt
@tenantUserToken = replace-with-tenant-user-jwt
@productId = 1
@moduleId = 1
@featureId = 1
@actionId = 1
@tenantId = 1
@membershipId = 1

# After tenant registration, copy the returned tenant ID into @tenantId. After each login, copy
# the returned accessToken into @ownerToken or @tenantUserToken before sending protected requests.

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Public tenant registration (first member becomes TenantAdmin; selects one or more seeded products)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register-tenant-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantKey": "acme",
  "tenantName": "Acme Ltd",
  "displayName": "Avery Admin",
  "email": "admin@acme.example",
  "password": "change-this-long-password-123",
  "productIds": [1]
}

### Tenant admin login (select the tenant to get a tenant-scoped JWT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@acme.example",
  "password": "change-this-long-password-123",
  "tenantId": {{tenantId}}
}

### Tenant admin creates a tenant user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Jamie User",
  "email": "jamie@acme.example",
  "password": "change-this-long-password-456"
}

### Tenant user login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jamie@acme.example",
  "password": "change-this-long-password-456",
  "tenantId": {{tenantId}}
}

### Verify the authenticated subject and roles from a JWT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### List active products for signup
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?status=Active&page=1&pageSize=50
Accept: application/json

### Create a module under the product (admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{productId}}/modules
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "invoices",
  "name": "Invoices",
  "sortOrder": 1
}

### Create a feature under the module (admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{productId}}/modules/{{moduleId}}/features
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "invoice-records",
  "name": "Invoice records",
  "sortOrder": 1
}

### Create an action on the feature (admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{productId}}/modules/{{moduleId}}/features/{{featureId}}/actions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "export",
  "name": "Export"
}

### List the authenticated user's tenants and active product subscriptions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Subscribe an existing tenant to a product (admin; idempotent)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/product-subscriptions/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### List tenant product subscriptions (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/product-subscriptions?status=Active&page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### List tenant memberships (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships?status=Active&page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Grant a feature action to the tenant membership (admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}/actions/{{actionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### List actions assigned to a membership (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}/actions?productId={{productId}}&isActive=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### List the authenticated user's effective actions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/me/actions?productId={{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Check whether the authenticated user may perform this action
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/authorization/check
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productKey": "erp",
  "moduleKey": "invoices",
  "featureKey": "invoice-records",
  "actionKey": "export"
}

### Revoke the action; repeating the access check should return allowed=false
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}/actions/{{actionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### This should return allowed=false with action_not_assigned
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/authorization/check
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productKey": "erp",
  "moduleKey": "invoices",
  "featureKey": "invoice-records",
  "actionKey": "export"
}

### Attempting to cancel the tenant's final active product must return 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/product-subscriptions/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Cancelled",
  "expiresAtUtc": null
}
